{
  "name": "09 · Competitor Change Monitor & Alerting (Intelligence)",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 09 · Competitor Change Monitor & Alerting\n**What it does:** On a schedule, fetches each tracked competitor's page (pricing, features, homepage), compares against the last snapshot, and if something changed, AI summarizes WHAT changed and WHY it matters → alerts Slack.\n\n**Why it sells:** Agencies & SaaS teams manually check competitor pricing/features weekly. This automates it and surfaces only meaningful changes. **Sell at:** $400-700 setup + $150-250/mo.",
        "height": 140,
        "width": 940,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "s9-title",
      "name": "Sticky: Title & ROI",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -360,
        -260
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### Targets\n**Schedule:** daily at 7 AM.\n**Demo:** manual trigger with sample competitor list.\n\nEach target: name, URL, page type (pricing/features/home).\nValidate: URL format, page type in allowed list.",
        "height": 200,
        "width": 300,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "s9-input",
      "name": "Sticky: Targets",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -360,
        -80
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### Fetch + Diff\n1. HTTP GET the competitor page\n2. Extract text content\n3. Load last snapshot from Sheets\n4. Compute a content hash + simple diff\n5. If hash unchanged → skip (no alert)\n6. If changed → pass to AI\n\nIdempotency: hash-based, won't re-alert on identical content.",
        "height": 200,
        "width": 340,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "s9-fetch",
      "name": "Sticky: Fetch + Diff",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        160,
        -80
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### AI Summary + Alert\n- Gemini summarizes WHAT changed + business impact\n- Confidence gate: low-confidence → flag for manual review\n- Slack alert with change summary + link\n- Save new snapshot to Sheets\n\nOnly meaningful changes trigger alerts. Noise filtered.",
        "height": 200,
        "width": 340,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "s9-ai",
      "name": "Sticky: AI Summary + Alert",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1180,
        -80
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "rule": {
          "interval": [
            {
              "field": "cronExpression",
              "expression": "0 7 * * *"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "s9-schedule",
      "name": "Schedule: Daily 7AM",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.scheduleTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        -320,
        20
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {},
      "id": "s9-manual",
      "name": "Manual Trigger",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.manualTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -320,
        200
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForAllItems",
        "jsCode": "\n// Demo competitor list. PRODUCTION: replace with Sheets read of a \"Competitors\" tab.\nconst targets = [\n  { name: \"Competitor A\", url: \"https://example.com/pricing\", pageType: \"pricing\" },\n  { name: \"Competitor B\", url: \"https://example.org/features\", pageType: \"features\" }\n];\nconst allowed = [\"pricing\", \"features\", \"home\"];\nreturn targets.map(t => ({ json: { ...t, EventKey: \"competitor:\" + t.name + \":\" + new Date().toISOString().slice(0,10) } }));\n"
      },
      "id": "s9-targets",
      "name": "Competitor Targets (Demo)",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        -60,
        100
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForEachItem",
        "jsCode": "\nconst t = $json;\nconst allowed = [\"pricing\", \"features\", \"home\"];\nlet urlOk = false;\ntry { new URL(t.url); urlOk = true; } catch(e) {}\nconst ok = urlOk && t.name && allowed.includes(t.pageType);\nif (!ok) return { json: { Timestamp: new Date().toISOString(), EventKey: t.EventKey || 'unknown',\n  Workflow: 'competitor-monitor', Status: 'rejected_invalid_target', Reason: 'bad URL or pageType' } };\nreturn { json: { ...t, input_valid: true } };\n"
      },
      "id": "s9-validate",
      "name": "Validate Target",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        200,
        100
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "leftValue": "",
            "typeValidation": "strict",
            "version": 2
          },
          "conditions": [
            {
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.input_valid === true }}",
              "rightValue": "",
              "operator": {
                "type": "boolean",
                "operation": "true",
                "singleValue": true
              }
            }
          ],
          "combinator": "and"
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "s9-if-valid",
      "name": "Target Valid?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        460,
        100
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "method": "GET",
        "url": "={{ $json.url }}",
        "options": {
          "response": {
            "response": {
              "responseFormat": "text"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "id": "s9-fetch",
      "name": "HTTP: Fetch Page",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [
        720,
        20
      ],
      "retryOnFail": true,
      "maxTries": 3,
      "waitBetweenTries": 3000
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForEachItem",
        "jsCode": "\nconst target = $('Validate Target').item.json;\nconst html = typeof $json === 'string' ? $json : ($json.data || $json.body || JSON.stringify($json));\n// Strip HTML tags + whitespace to get content text\nconst text = String(html).replace(/<script[\\s\\S]*?<\\/script>/gi, '')\n  .replace(/<style[\\s\\S]*?<\\/style>/gi, '')\n  .replace(/<[^>]+>/g, ' ')\n  .replace(/\\s+/g, ' ').trim();\n// Simple hash (djb2)\nlet hash = 5381;\nfor (let i = 0; i < text.length; i++) { hash = ((hash << 5) + hash + text.charCodeAt(i)) >>> 0; }\nconst contentHash = String(hash);\n// PRODUCTION: load last snapshot hash from Sheets \"Competitor Snapshots\" tab.\n// Demo: assume last hash differs so the flow continues to AI.\nconst lastHash = null; // PRODUCTION: Sheets lookup by competitor name\nconst changed = lastHash !== contentHash;\nreturn { json: { ...target, contentText: text.slice(0, 8000), contentHash, lastHash, changed } };\n"
      },
      "id": "s9-diff",
      "name": "Extract + Hash + Diff",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        980,
        20
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "leftValue": "",
            "typeValidation": "strict",
            "version": 2
          },
          "conditions": [
            {
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.changed === true }}",
              "rightValue": "",
              "operator": {
                "type": "boolean",
                "operation": "true",
                "singleValue": true
              }
            }
          ],
          "combinator": "and"
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "s9-if-changed",
      "name": "Content Changed?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        1240,
        20
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "modelId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "id",
          "value": "models/gemma-4-31b-it"
        },
        "messages": {
          "values": [
            {
              "content": "=You are a competitive intelligence analyst. A competitor's {{ $json.pageType }} page changed. Summarize what likely changed and the business impact for a competing team.\n\nCOMPETITOR: {{ $json.name }}\nPAGE TYPE: {{ $json.pageType }}\nCURRENT CONTENT (truncated):\n{{ $json.contentText }}\n\nGenerate exactly this JSON (no markdown fences):\n{\n  \"summary\": \"<2-3 sentence summary of what this page offers / what likely changed>\",\n  \"key_points\": [\"<point 1>\", \"<point 2>\", \"<point 3>\"],\n  \"business_impact\": \"<one sentence on what a competing team should do>\",\n  \"confidence\": <0.0-1.0>\n}\nYour ENTIRE response must be that single JSON object."
            }
          ]
        },
        "builtInTools": {},
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "s9-gemini",
      "name": "Gemini: Summarize Change",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.googleGemini",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        1500,
        -60
      ],
      "credentials": {
        "googlePalmApi": {
          "id": "B8oepyrWrBGFl6Ud",
          "name": "Google Gemini (portfolio)"
        }
      },
      "retryOnFail": true,
      "maxTries": 3,
      "waitBetweenTries": 3000
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForEachItem",
        "jsCode": "\nconst raw = $json.content?.parts?.filter(p => !p.thought).map(p => p.text || '').join('') ?? $json.text ?? '';\nconst cleaned = raw.replace(/```json/gi,'').replace(/```/g,'').trim();\nlet data = null;\nfor (const c of (cleaned.match(/\\{[\\s\\S]*\\}/g) || []).reverse()) {\n  try { const p = JSON.parse(c); if (p && p.summary) { data = p; break; } } catch(e){}\n}\nconst target = $('Extract + Hash + Diff').item.json;\nif (!data) return { json: { ...target, parse_ok: false, error: 'AI output unparseable' } };\nconst confidence = typeof data.confidence === 'number' ? data.confidence : 0.7;\nreturn { json: { ...target, ...data, confidence, parse_ok: true } };\n"
      },
      "id": "s9-parse",
      "name": "Parse Summary",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        1760,
        -60
      ]
